From: Johann Hartmann <johann@mayflower.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: clear closed substream for fixed IRQs

The fixed IRQ remains reserved across closes, but its ALSA substream does
not. Retaining that borrowed pointer after close blocks checked DSP SRAM
retirement and leaves a pointer to a freed PCM on MT8901. Clear it for both
IRQ allocation modes. Keep the fixed IRQ reservation intact.

--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-afe-fe-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-afe-fe-dai.c
@@ -113,8 +113,9 @@
 	if (!memif->const_irq) {
 		mtk_dynamic_irq_release(afe, irq_id);
 		memif->irq_usage = -1;
-		memif->substream = NULL;
-	}
+	}
+	/* A fixed IRQ reservation outlives the PCM, its borrower does not. */
+	memif->substream = NULL;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mtk_afe_fe_shutdown);
 
